            <div xml:id="d330">

                <pb facs="0412" n="404" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg404"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">362.115/337: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-11-21T16:00:00+01:00">November 21, 1938—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 21—12:22 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>643. Reference Embassy’s 621, November 15, 7 p.m., paragraph <hi
                        rendition="#italic">c</hi> and 626, November 16, 6 p.m., paragraph 3.</p>
                <p>I have presented a note under today’s date to the German Foreign Office in which,
                    with reference to the decree of the German Government of November 12 for the
                    termination on January 1, 1939 of the <pb facs="0413" n="405" xml:id="pg405"/>
                    right of Jews to engage in various commercial activities, there is cited the
                    statement of the German Minister of Propaganda and Public Enlightenment on
                    November 12 to the effect that the various recent decrees affecting German Jews
                    would not be applicable to Jews of foreign nationality and formal assurances are
                    requested that the decree in question would not apply to American citizens.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
